  "reason": "No experiments have been completed yet, so the highest-priority need is to establish a clear performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space: a single modality, single profile, and a linear (PCA) encoder with no aggregation or fusion. Running this first gives a well-defined performance floor against which every subsequent design choice—stronger RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation (avgpool, transformer), image modality, and multimodal fusion—can be measured. It also isolates the contribution of the PCA representation before any other variable is introduced, so that later experiments can cleanly attribute performance changes to specific design decisions rather than conflating multiple factors. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search with the most minimal, interpretable baseline is the most information-efficient first step."
